-- EIGHTY MORE BOARDS PRINT THE NAME THEIR EMPLOYER USES.
--
-- Trust round 3 (owner decisions of 2026-10-25 and 2026-10-26: pages carry
-- true names, true countries and true agency labels, and a gate is never
-- loosened to get there). The census tools named many boards after a label:
-- an ADP logo file ("HRH Secaucus University Transparent", "mc cmyk (3)"),
-- an Ashby page title ("Jobs"), a Greenhouse board title ("Job Board", "Only
-- External Postings", a bare region), an Oracle or UKG site label ("HKBU
-- e-Recruitment System", "Recruiting 2025"). The bake's name gate lets most of
-- them through, so a posting page would print the label as its hirer.
--
-- WHERE EACH NAME CAME FROM. The employer's own words for itself, read gently
-- (one request a second per host) on 2026-10-25 (the agency round,
-- ~/.config/resumebooster/agency-flags-2026-10-25) or 2026-10-26 (the round-2
-- plan and this round's re-reads, ~/.config/resumebooster/trust-round-2): a
-- posting's own text, the vendor's own name field for the board (Greenhouse
-- boards-api name, Rippling companyName, BambooHR og:site_name), an Oracle
-- site's SiteName and a requisition's text, or the employer's own careers page
-- linking the board. Every row has its links and the words read in
-- public.company_name_evidence (20261025100000 made it; only the service role
-- reads it). Nothing is guessed: a board whose words did not name its employer
-- keeps its stored name (ADP "Screenshot", "No Background", "AH transparent
-- (3)", "OH horz transparent" and the HelloWellness / brello board; Ashby's
-- seven empty "Jobs" boards; Lever's "APPLY", which the gate refuses as a word
-- and which the employer now calls itself; Oracle's Dallah Recruitment System,
-- whose group name is shared by several companies). Not censused at all, and
-- many: at least 71 more ADP and UKG boards still print a logo file or a file
-- path ("BradfordHealthServicesLogo Revised Blue LeftAlignedHR", a "C:Users..."
-- path), 1,021 open roles between them on 2026-10-26 by the review's read
-- (~/.config/resumebooster/trust-round-3-fixes/junk-counts-review-2026-10-26.json),
-- for a later census round; this file names none of them.
--
-- TWO WRITERS, BY TOKEN SHAPE. A token carrying a "~" (an Oracle or UKG site,
-- an ADP client with a career-center id) takes a company_name_overrides row
-- below, which trg_company_name_override applies to every write and
-- src/lib/employer-names.ts mirrors for the bake and the app. A bare token (a
-- Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, BambooHR, Rippling or Teamtailor board, an ADP
-- client id alone) cannot take an override, so its catalogue entry is renamed
-- in job-board's sources.ts (and its byte-identical layoff-filings copy) and
-- listed in RENAMED_TOKENS; its evidence is kept here under vendor:token.
--
-- WHAT RENAMES THE STORED ROWS. Not this file (S11-133). job-board
-- 2026-09-09.96 moves NAME_SYNC_VERSION from 5 to 6, and its name-sync lane
-- then renames the stored postings, closures, snapshots and closure rollup a
-- board at a time: every board an override names and every token in
-- RENAMED_TOKENS. So this file is applied BEFORE job-board .96 deploys
-- (docs/deploy-ledger.json migrationOrder): applied after it, the lane can
-- finish version 6 before these overrides exist.
--
-- RE-RUNNABLE: ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE on both tables. No table is created
-- here, so no grant changes (company_name_evidence is already revoked from
-- anon and authenticated, and the self-check below says so again).

SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '10s';
SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '2min';

COMMENT ON TABLE public.company_name_evidence IS
  'Why a board carries its employer''s name: the links read and the employer''s own words. '
  'One row per company_name_overrides slug (a token with a "~"), from 20261025100000 on, and '
  'from 20261026100000 one row per catalogue rename, keyed vendor:token (no override slug holds a ":"). '
  'NOT client-readable: no client policy and no anon or authenticated grant.';

